": 3}

- {"summary": "The paper introduces NAIT (Neuron Activation-based Instruction Tuning), a novel framework for selecting high-quality instruction tuning (IT) data for large language models (LLMs) by analyzing neuron activation patterns. NAIT operates in two stages: Neuron Activation Feature Extraction and Activation Feature-Guided Data Selection. It outperforms existing methods like AlpaGasus and SelectIT, achieving up to 4.65% improvement in mathematical reasoning tasks and 3.24% overall improvement using only 10% of the original IT data. NAIT is cost-efficient, robust, and interpretable, but its scalability,", "significance_and_novelty": "NAIT introduces a novel approach to IT data selection by leveraging neuron activation patterns, offering a cost-efficient, interpretable, and robust method that outperforms existing techniques. It addresses the challenge of enhancing specific domain capabilities in LLMs without relying on external,", "reasons_for_acceptance": ["NAIT demonstrates significant performance improvements across multiple tasks, including mathematical reasoning and multilingual understanding, using only 10% of the original IT data.", "The method is cost-efficient, achieving up to 19\u00d7 cost reduction compared to AlpaGasus and 17.58\u00d7 speedup compared to SelectIT.", "NAIT provides strong interpretability, revealing logical reasoning and programmatic features that enhance model capabilities.", "The framework is robust, showing consistent performance across different base models, IT datasets, and domain-specific datasets."], "reasons_for_rejection": ["The analysis is limited to models with fewer than 20 billion parameters due to computational constraints, raising questions about scalability to larger models.", "The paper lacks a detailed ablation study on the impact of varying proportions of IT data on performance across different tasks.", "While NAIT outperforms existing methods, the paper does not thoroughly explore potential limitations or failure cases in specific domains or tasks."], "suggestions": ["Conduct a scalability study on larger models to validate the effectiveness of NAIT in more complex scenarios.", "Include a more detailed ablation study to understand the impact of different proportions of IT data on task performance.", "Explore potential limitations or failure cases of NAIT in specific domains or tasks to provide a more comprehensive evaluation.", "Provide additional insights into the transferability of neuron activation features across different capabilities and tasks."], "rating": 8, "confidence": 4, "soundness": 4, "presentation": 4, "contribution": 4}

